cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Diet Recommendation System: code for 'Translating Dietary Standards into Healthy Meals with Few-Ingredient Substitutions'"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
abstract: >-
  Code that reproduces the analyses of the article: meals built from the NHANES / What We Eat in
  America dietary recalls, 34 meal archetypes found with HDBSCAN, a conditional variational
  autoencoder that generates meals per archetype, portioning toward USDA targets, and one- to
  three-food substitutions evaluated for nutrition and cost.
keywords:
  - nutrition
  - meal generation
  - dietary recommendations
  - conditional variational autoencoder
  - NHANES
  - food substitution
authors:
